"""Concepts to teach before existing quizzes; no live questions or answer keys."""
BRIDGES={
2:('Execution order and saved changes','The number beside a code cell records when it ran in that session, not its position on the page. Restart clears memory; Run All follows page order. A fresh run tests the run order, not whether the engineering formula is valid. A commit is a recorded change. In terminal reference material, git status describes local changes; it does not itself save or upload them.'),
3:('Units branches and error messages','Read the unit beside each function input. Millimetres become metres by dividing by 1000. Percent becomes a fraction by dividing by 100. Rotational speed in rpm becomes radians per second by multiplying by 2π/60. These conversions change the number, not the physical quantity. In an if/elif chain, Python uses the FIRST matching branch. Trace one branch at a time. A TypeError can mean text was used where a number was expected. Put a repeated teaching limit in one clearly named constant.'),
4:('Counting every record honestly','DictReader already consumes the header; skipping its first yielded row skips real data. A string such as "unknown" cannot be converted to float. Catch the expected conversion error, count and record it, then continue under a stated policy. Inspect whether skipped rows share a source before reporting a mean. A sample summary describes observed records, not every possible operating condition.'),
5:('Data types and filters','A Boolean mask is a list-like column of True/False values. len(mask) counts all rows; mask.sum() counts True entries. Strings sort as text, so "9" can rank above "100". Inspect numeric types before taking maxima. KeyError often means the column name does not match; check spelling, case and spaces. shape is (rows, columns). Read provenance and units before trusting a dataset.'),
6:('Cleaning choices and charts','Filling blanks with zero changes the mean and may be unjustified. Dropping every row with any blank can remove valid observations. A failed numeric conversion identifies a problematic value to inspect rather than hide. A histogram describes one distribution; a scatter plot shows paired values; a grouped chart compares groups. Read both axes and units. A plausible extreme needs investigation before deletion.'),
8:('Reading model outputs','A score on training rows describes training fit. A feature table must preserve the training column names, order and units during prediction. A one-dimensional list may have the wrong shape for a model expecting rows and columns. A predicted-versus-actual plot uses the diagonal as perfect agreement; a pattern is not proof of causation. Judge MAE against the baseline and the decision’s acceptable error. R² is not an accuracy percentage.'),
9:('Category predictions and operating thresholds','A majority-only classifier can achieve high accuracy while missing the rare class. Name the positive class and both confusion-matrix axes. A model expecting numeric features cannot directly use raw category strings; demonstrate one-hot indicators before a fitting example. Compare threshold choices on validation data. Reducing the threshold adds flagged cases and cannot reduce recall on fixed scored observations, but precision can move either way.'),
10:('Interpreting validation results','Fit an imputer or scaler only on training data; putting it in a Pipeline helps enforce that during cross-validation. A low training error and high validation error suggest overfitting, but data shift or leakage can also matter. Missing predictor values need a stated treatment. Report fold scores and their variation, not just the best fold. Group related observations together when the deployment goal is new equipment.'),
11:('Features without misleading evaluation','Rescaling an input usually does not change the partitions available to an ordinary decision tree. An identifier or a future-known field can create an apparent improvement without useful predictive information. Dividing by zero can produce infinity or an error; decide what the denominator means before replacing it. Read ablation differences using the same error definition, and explain features using domain knowledge.'),
12:('Fair comparison and explanation','Compare the same metric on the same validation cases with the same preprocessing rules. A small difference needs context, including variation across splits. Code run out of order can overwrite the variable holding a model; restart and run from the top. A local explanation addresses one prediction; global importance summarises many. A post-hoc explanation of a complex model is not its directly readable internal rule.'),
13:('A reproducible handover','An absolute path from your own computer will usually fail elsewhere. A relative path starts from the current working folder. Record dependencies and actual versions, and fix randomness where appropriate; identical results across all machines are not guaranteed by a seed alone. Captions should state a supported finding and its scope. Remove conflicting cell assignments and verify a fresh run before submission.')}
